  "observations": [
    "Each pinned engine passes 94 group/pointer/label rows and 29 whole native member comparisons. Native actions cover implicit/explicit nested labels, selected members, retargeted labels and cancelled forwarded clicks. Original disabled/interactive/cancelled/removed-target/text-drag filtering remains. Programmatic model changes preserve native images.",
    "Each native label action is recorded as semantic performClick without a fabricated native pointer press. The engine constructs the original trusted PointerEvent with mouse source; original input/change events and cancellation rollback remain intact.",
    "Final ordinary AppKit matrix comparisons pass 312 rows/34 complete images at actual 1x/2x backing. Typed wire checks pass 163/42, including full-width identities, native callbacks, busy/disabled/unknown/malformed/foreign-connection rejection. A separate ordinary NSButton comparison passes 27 actions over button/check/radio kinds and off/on/mixed initial states, with callback destruction/reentry guards.",
    "Current button/text regressions pass Firefox 108/48 and Chromium 107/48. The full shared NativeUI provider/transport suite and older client/loader regression pass. A new loader with the actual older 520-byte provider reports semantic activation unsupported and remains usable.",
    "An early host rejected the existing nonzero sequence field as unused; raw traces show suppressed label activation and no native action. The owner-validated final operation preserves the sequence. The failed host source and traces remain diagnostic evidence.",
    "Initial provider observations either ran the old test executable or stopped at stale fixed image totals. A later disabled-image mismatch came from a reference enabled flag left true. Final native references use the same intended enabled model; provider behavior was unchanged. Transport image totals were likewise updated for the added semantic cases.",
    "The first Firefox broad run supplies original count 1 on the second physical click and fails the intended double-click assertion. Final test dispatches the three real seat clicks without intermediate state queries, still requires actual engine counts 1/2/3, and passes both engines. The earlier failure is retained separately.",
    "A new C input test incorrectly assumed a momentary button state resets to zero after performClick. It was replaced by the independent ordinary NSButton comparison, which matches actual native behavior without corrective provider code. The failed test/run remain archived."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Non-radio browser label bindings, label pressed-state/animation coverage, accessibility activation and broader author-style/complex-control cases.",
    "Radio topology beyond one column, visibility/geometry variants, large-group efficiency, browser zoom/other scales/builds, native double-action timing and actual session-supervisor group recovery.",
    "Remaining browser controls and complete detached-menu/native-shortcut integration, accessibility/IME, derivatives and installed deployment. GTK/Qt/KDE follow the browser work through the same shared layer.",
    "Browser toolbar/address bar/tabs keep their current components; future requested UI changes use optional per-app patches above the shared library and bridge."
  ],
  "source_audit": "radio-label-source-audit.json"
}
